, I thought I read it somewhere and you are correct.<br /> <br /> In the GerDiv and Magadon sections alone, there were at least four instances of Pentex making &quot;mutants&quot; WITHOUT the use of banes. Period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:45:58-07:00","id":1137794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1137625#post1137625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex makes Formori by putting toxic waste barrels in creeks.<br /> <br /> It can make Formori with surgery and injections.<br /> <br /> It doesn't go for the torch-lit ceremony thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I didn't say it did. Also, what you described is not really a science, but just another manifestation of making deals or attracting spirits, which is also why I bristle at the notion of Garou necessarily being religious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:54:17-07:00","id":1137797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1137794#post1137794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I didn't say it did. Also, what you described is not really a science, but just another manifestation of making deals or attracting spirits, which is also why I bristle at the notion of Garou necessarily being religious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou are explictly a religious military order. They can't NOT be religious and be part of the Garou Nation since the Garou Nation is a military order dedicated to defending God.<br /> <br /> It's just God is the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T17:03:22-07:00","id":1137869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1137797#post1137797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Garou are explictly a religious military order.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not. They're spirit warriors who band together into septs and have a number of strong disagreements with each other, the only thing they don't disagree about being the importance of standing against corruption for Gaia, as they can all get the feeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can't NOT be religious and be part of the Garou Nation since the Garou Nation is a military order dedicated to defending God.<br /> <br /> It's just God is the universe. </div> </div> </div>Pages 36-40 of the Revised Storyteller's Handbook outline how that tack is extremely misleading. It also mentions that there are religious factions in the Garou Nation - not a single whole, but a number of different takes on things when it comes to organized belief, as opposed to ritual ceremonies to appease beings that you can touch and talk with. You absolutely do not need to treat it as a religion. The Uktena and Stargazers sure don't; the dissection of mystic lore that they engage in tends to lends itself much more to philosophical takes than religious ones. Meanwhile, the Bone Gnawers are largerly too concerned with survival to bother with religious dimensions of animism over practical ones, while Glass Walkers only really have a religious faction in the form of the Wise Guys, who mix in a lot of Catholicism, not unlike the Sisters of Our Merciful Mother, from the Black Furies' corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T21:01:02-07:00","id":1137911,"title":"","content":"The....STARGAZERS don't treat themselves as a religious order? The werewolves who are a practicing monastic Buddhist religious order?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://theidlesherpa.files.wordpress.com/2011/07/wtf_look.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T18:36:28-07:00","id":1138171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1137911#post1137911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The....STARGAZERS don't treat themselves as a religious order? The werewolves who are a practicing monastic Buddhist religious order?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be The Zephyr camp, specifically. If you're in a different camp, or not in a camp at all, you won't share the same outlook. See also, Stargazers Revised page 32 for a direct refutation of your assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T00:55:49-07:00","id":1142064,"title":"","content":"Werewolves give Chimanage to numerous spirits, especially their pack totem, Cairn Totems, Luna and Gaia in many rites.<br /> It is religious in nature because they worship spirits, but it's Animism or Shamanism faith, an older more primal type of religion. you'll find that most practices are the same or similar around the world (With changes not unlike denominations of Christianity)<br /> But it's definitely religious, monthly midnight masses (moot) at the local church (Cairn) Literally fighting the archenemy (Wyrm) and their minions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:14:35-07:00","id":1142250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142064#post1142064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves give Chimanage to numerous spirits, especially their pack totem, Cairn Totems, Luna and Gaia in many rites.<br /> It is religious in nature because they worship spirits, but it's Animism or Shamanism faith, an older more primal type of religion. you'll find that most practices are the same or similar around the world (With changes not unlike denominations of Christianity)<br /> But it's definitely religious, monthly midnight masses (moot) at the local church (Cairn) Literally fighting the archenemy (Wyrm) and their minions</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't actually worship spirits, or at least, that sort of mindset is not required for working the traditions in a rite. Chiminage is a deal struck in good faith, not veneration in the faith of a religion. Also, moots are often even more like war councils in flavor, and the sacred grounds where vitality leaks through to still nourish the world in a very palpable fashion. Whatever religious significance or approach clings to these practices tends to come from the upbringing of a Homid Garou, to the extent that it survives or manages to mesh well with the practices of the Garou as distinct from humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:34:28-07:00","id":1142264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142250#post1142250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't actually worship spirits, or at least, that sort of mindset is not required for working the traditions in a rite. Chiminage is a deal struck in good faith, not veneration in the faith of a religion. Also, moots are often even more like war councils in flavor, and the sacred grounds where vitality leaks through to still nourish the world in a very palpable fashion. Whatever religious significance or approach clings to these practices tends to come from the upbringing of a Homid Garou, to the extent that it survives or manages to mesh well with the practices of the Garou as distinct from humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all worship is about faith-veneration. A lot of religious (e.g. Chinese folk religion[s]) treat 'just business' relationships with deities as a normal thing. To think otherwise sounds like leaning towards a mix of Abrahamo- and post-antiquity-Eurocentrism (not the best term, I know, but hopefully it's good enough to make the point across).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:45:48-07:00","id":1142268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142264#post1142264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all worship is about faith-veneration. A lot of religious (e.g. Chinese folk religion[s]) treat 'just business' relationships with deities as a normal thing. To think otherwise sounds like leaning towards a mix of Abrahamo- and post-antiquity-Eurocentrism (not the best term, I know, but hopefully it's good enough to make the point across).</div> </div> </div> </div>Worship has a very specific meaning within common use of English and it having been shaped by its formation within Christian cultures in Europe, though. Also, the distinction was drawn in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, which does make bones about beings religious vs. being spiritual, and how while all Garou are the latter (because they are part spirit and live with spirits and can touch them), they are not universally the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T17:36:51-07:00","id":1142355,"title":"","content":"I would still see it as religion, but I can concede your view when looking through a slightly different lens.<br /> The weird thing would be &quot;Faith&quot; Wolves don't have faith because they can interact with these godly creatures and directly see the results","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T23:36:47-07:00","id":1142428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142355#post1142355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing would be &quot;Faith&quot; Wolves don't have faith because they can interact with these godly creatures and directly see the results</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Gaia, and the Triat? Very, very few (near to none, I think?) Fera actually interact with them directly. Yet the Garou base - or try to base - their actions on their for love Gaia. Isn't this faith?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you say that the Ananasi have no faith in Queen Ananasa because they interact with her personally? I think they do; unless they are one of the ones that don't follow Queen Ananasa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-21-2017, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T00:16:47-07:00","id":1142430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142268#post1142268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worship has a very specific meaning within common use of English and it having been shaped by its formation within Christian cultures in Europe, though. Also, the distinction was drawn in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, which does make bones about beings religious vs. being spiritual, and how while all Garou are the latter (because they are part spirit and live with spirits and can touch them), they are not universally the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>That . . . sort of plays into a very Euro kind of No True Scotsman against other types of religions.<br /> It sort of reminds me how to an east-derived culture person, Kappa are water deities, but I've seen euro-derived-culture people saying that they &quot;don't count&quot; as 'true' deities and thus believing in Kappa does not make one religious.<br /> <br /> I'm pointing it out because Werewolf is supposed to be more international and tribal, so such a 'Western' form of NTSing looks very out of place and contrary the aforementioned aspect of the game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","user":"vicky_molokh","date":". 09-21-2017, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:21:37-07:00","id":1142696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142430#post1142430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That . . . sort of plays into a very Euro kind of No True Scotsman against other types of religions.<br /> It sort of reminds me how to an east-derived culture person, Kappa are water deities, but I've seen euro-derived-culture people saying that they &quot;don't count&quot; as 'true' deities and thus believing in Kappa does not make one religious.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Garou and Fera don't believe in these, because <i>they exist independently of belief</i>. Changers and others attuned to the Middle Umbra touch and feel and know that something is there. There is no question of faith in a (culturally plundered) all-powerful figure as in Christianity; none of the world beyond is ineffable, abstract, or an allegory. The forces are palpable in Werewolf. You can touch them, and they can touch back. Ironically, having faith tends to make them less able to do so, because you have faith in a human belief system, and they don't tend to match up with the realities of the Penumbra of the WoD, instead granting the True Faith trait and blocking out most living spirits and ghosts via established human spiritual practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pointing it out because Werewolf is supposed to be more international and tribal, so such a 'Western' form of NTSing looks very out of place and contrary the aforementioned aspect of the game line. </div> </div> </div>It's similarly international in how it tends to disregard what a lot of religions consider important, using the broader version of the term religion. No one's beliefs are going to line up with those of the Garou or Fera to any secure degree, because firstly, that wouldn't make them very horrifying worldwide when they need to be in a metatextual capacity of purpose (if werewolves aren't scary in some way to someone, why bother?), and secondly, Werewolf has a big thing about rejecting humanity putting itself on a pedestal, which is going to be present in most, if not all, religions to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:28:55-07:00","id":1142698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142428#post1142428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Gaia, and the Triat? Very, very few (near to none, I think?) Fera actually interact with them directly. Yet the Garou base - or try to base - their actions on their for love Gaia. Isn't this faith?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's impossible to interact with Gaia and the Triat directly, in the same sense that it's impossible for a tiny being such as one of us to interact with the Solar System or Galaxy on a whole, much less something that permeates and feeds into the existence of all space-time. However, anyone with Gnosis can feel their connection to the cosmos, not unlike how Jedi or the psychics from Trinity are attuned to the universe and all life within it. They don't receive these cues in an uncertain fashion, much as how Obi Wan was not wholly uncertain about what happened to Alderaan in Episode 4. A lot of people died. The exact cause might have been up for discussion until they ran into the Death Star, but the event itself? There was only the cold, stomach-turning, horrifying certainty that it happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you say that the Ananasi have no faith in Queen Ananasa because they interact with her personally? I think they do; unless they are one of the ones that don't follow Queen Ananasa. </div> </div> </div>They pulled a massive campaign of deceit and manipulation to be able to talk to her and find a way out of the present FUBAR state of the universe, so that's not really something I would place as faith in a religious sense. They have great faith that she knows what she's doing, and being away from her is likely what could be classified as &quot;spiritually taxing&quot;, but that's a different sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T15:22:50-07:00","id":1142720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142696#post1142696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Garou and Fera don't believe in these, because <i>they exist independently of belief</i>. Changers and others attuned to the Middle Umbra touch and feel and know that something is there. There is no question of faith in a (culturally plundered) all-powerful figure as in Christianity; none of the world beyond is ineffable, abstract, or an allegory. The forces are palpable in Werewolf. You can touch them, and they can touch back. Ironically, having faith tends to make them less able to do so, because you have faith in a human belief system, and they don't tend to match up with the realities of the Penumbra of the WoD, instead granting the True Faith trait and blocking out most living spirits and ghosts via established human spiritual practices.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's similarly international in how it tends to disregard what a lot of religions consider important, using the broader version of the term religion. No one's beliefs are going to line up with those of the Garou or Fera to any secure degree, because firstly, that wouldn't make them very horrifying worldwide when they need to be in a metatextual capacity of purpose (if werewolves aren't scary in some way to someone, why bother?), and secondly, Werewolf has a big thing about rejecting humanity putting itself on a pedestal, which is going to be present in most, if not all, religions to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>...as a member of Asatru (Norse Heathenry), a religion that is based on an animist worldview, I find that my beliefs match up fairly well with the Garou actually. I obviously disagree with the Get of Fenris on a couple points but that everything has a spirit/soul/consciousness and that entropy/chaos/evil are represented by a class of spirits that can be fought and defeated (Thursar) are big similarities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T19:56:07-07:00","id":1142789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142720#post1142720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...as a member of Asatru (Norse Heathenry), a religion that is based on an animist worldview, I find that my beliefs match up fairly well with the Garou actually. I obviously disagree with the Get of Fenris on a couple points but that everything has a spirit/soul/consciousness and that entropy/chaos/evil are represented by a class of spirits that can be fought and defeated (Thursar) are big similarities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I think you might be a bit off on the representation of a twisted cosmos, which can't really be defeated just by defeating a few, or even a myriad of, jotun. This is actually one of the big things about Werewolf as a whole - tackling strategic problems rather than perpetually concentrating on tactical ones, thus making a greater difference in the war at the cost of personal recognition within the culture. You'll be fighting less often, but accomplishing more; trying to get into the warrior's glorious afterlife is a goal that you'll have to set aside if you want to actually make a difference.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the points where the Get of Fenris diverge seem like they would be pretty big. Wotan in Werewolf is an evil necromancer, and possibly also a vampire. The Aesir and Vanir are disdained as enemies, of whom only a few gain recognition as powerful or notable in a fight, which is where the respect of the Fenrir ends. Also, they might be ghouls. Fenris will eventually slay Wotan, and this is presented as a good thing. Also, the cause of eclipses? It doesn't seem to have anything to do with Fenris, who is also not a child of Loki (the Revised Tribebook made a salty statement of humans confusing &quot;image conjured by Loki&quot; with &quot;created/born by Loki&quot;). Also, if we're going by the antagonist nature of the Aesir and Vanir here, they seem to be on the side of the thursar, or at least indifferent to the evil they wreak in the world. Also, the Fenrir killed a bunch of Asatru when they purged the Swords of Heimdall from their ranks.<br /> <br /> Werewolf doesn't really have a setting that exists to validate human beliefs. That;s where it gets most of its placement in the horror genre; everything you knew as a human prior to your change is at least sorely mistaken in some fashion, and likely to be flipped on its head. The wolf is the hero; the flock has eaten the mountain and forests and must be stopped. The dragon is keeping the living history of the world; those who come to slay her deserve the death by fire that they get when they intrude on her wallow. The serpent made an error in trusting someone, once, and now must secret herself away from the world of humans and strike at its most outstanding evils. If the tiger disregards its nature and tries to be human, it will bring ruin down on all tigers. And, finally, you root for the shark, because you know that Peter Benchley regretted what happened after the novel hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T00:39:43-07:00","id":1142825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142789#post1142789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, I think you might be a bit off on the representation of a twisted cosmos, which can't really be defeated just by defeating a few, or even a myriad of, jotun. This is actually one of the big things about Werewolf as a whole - tackling strategic problems rather than perpetually concentrating on tactical ones, thus making a greater difference in the war at the cost of personal recognition within the culture. You'll be fighting less often, but accomplishing more; trying to get into the warrior's glorious afterlife is a goal that you'll have to set aside if you want to actually make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was refering to defeating them on an individual level. I'm well aware that killing the Wyrm is as possible as preventing Ragnarok.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142789#post1142789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, the points where the Get of Fenris diverge seem like they would be pretty big. Wotan in Werewolf is an evil necromancer, and possibly also a vampire. The Aesir and Vanir are disdained as enemies, of whom only a few gain recognition as powerful or notable in a fight, which is where the respect of the Fenrir ends. Also, they might be ghouls. Fenris will eventually slay Wotan, and this is presented as a good thing. Also, the cause of eclipses? It doesn't seem to have anything to do with Fenris, who is also not a child of Loki (the Revised Tribebook made a salty statement of humans confusing &quot;image conjured by Loki&quot; with &quot;created/born by Loki&quot;). Also, if we're going by the antagonist nature of the Aesir and Vanir here, they seem to be on the side of the thursar, or at least indifferent to the evil they wreak in the world. Also, the Fenrir killed a bunch of Asatru when they purged the Swords of Heimdall from their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of the 1st ed version but even the revised take on Get beliefs agrees on the basic make up of the world that we have already gone over. Spirits of the land, sky, tablet computor etc. They just worship a different group of spirits. Even irl people worship the Vanir or Jotuns instead of and as well as the Aesir. To say nothing of other, more popular religions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142789#post1142789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf doesn't really have a setting that exists to validate human beliefs. That;s where it gets most of its placement in the horror genre; everything you knew as a human prior to your change is at least sorely mistaken in some fashion, and likely to be flipped on its head. The wolf is the hero; the flock has eaten the mountain and forests and must be stopped. The dragon is keeping the living history of the world; those who come to slay her deserve the death by fire that they get when they intrude on her wallow. The serpent made an error in trusting someone, once, and now must secret herself away from the world of humans and strike at its most outstanding evils. If the tiger disregards its nature and tries to be human, it will bring ruin down on all tigers. And, finally, you root for the shark, because you know that Peter Benchley regretted what happened after the novel hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think our differences in opinion come down to some very fundimentaly different takes on the setting. Werewolf just strikes me as a tragic setting more then a horror one. In that you are empowered but that power is ultimately worthless against the true enemy and your doomed to fail. I don't find any personal horror in being a Fera, &quot;So I'm a holy warrior for nature? Corporate suits really are out to destroy the world and I have to stop them? I get super powers? Sign me up!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T00:47:41-07:00","id":1142829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142696#post1142696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Garou and Fera don't believe in these, because <i>they exist independently of belief</i>. Changers and others attuned to the Middle Umbra touch and feel and know that something is there. There is no question of faith in a (culturally plundered) all-powerful figure as in Christianity; none of the world beyond is ineffable, abstract, or an allegory. The forces are palpable in Werewolf. You can touch them, and they can touch back. Ironically, having faith tends to make them less able to do so, because you have faith in a human belief system, and they don't tend to match up with the realities of the Penumbra of the WoD, instead granting the True Faith trait and blocking out most living spirits and ghosts via established human spiritual practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Existence independently of belief is mostly orthogonal to religion.<br /> Taking Moses' word as true, Moses saw proof of YHWH existing independently of his belief; does that make Moses irreligious or unfaithful? No, because otherwise you're forced to discard lots and lots of key figures in religions as irreligious/unfaithful.<br /> Conversely, I have faith that what my senses tell me about the existence of an outside world to be <i>somewhat</i> true. If I had no faith in that, I would be a solipsist. But again, that does not make me religious about, say, my ability to see this keyboard I'm typing with.<br /> <br /> Just because Garou religion is not at all similar to Abrahamic religions, but rather to animistic and other religions that treat relationships with deities as a more egalitarian affair, does not make Garou irreligious. In fact to dismiss Garou ways as irreligious is to go No True Scotsman on huge swathes of non-'Western' religions (and surely some of the older 'Western' ones), particularly most animistic ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142696#post1142696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's similarly international in how it tends to disregard what a lot of religions consider important, using the broader version of the term religion. No one's beliefs are going to line up with those of the Garou or Fera to any secure degree, because firstly, that wouldn't make them very horrifying worldwide when they need to be in a metatextual capacity of purpose (if werewolves aren't scary in some way to someone, why bother?), and secondly, Werewolf has a big thing about rejecting humanity putting itself on a pedestal, which is going to be present in most, if not all, religions to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of that seems to disqualify them of being religious. They just follow a religion that differs from human ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","user":"vicky_molokh","date":". 09-22-2017, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T08:53:01-07:00","id":1142924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142825#post1142825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was refering to defeating them on an individual level. I'm well aware that killing the Wyrm is as possible as preventing Ragnarok.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But correcting its ailment was apparently possible in that one Apocalypse scenario... provided that you were allies with Gurahl and brought along other Fera to help find the way to the proper ritual space with the least amount of fights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking of the 1st ed version </div> </div> </div>That's nowhere near the frame that the Fenrir work with now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but even the revised take on Get beliefs agrees on the basic make up of the world that we have already gone over. Spirits of the land, sky, tablet computor etc. They just worship a different group of spirits. Even irl people worship the Vanir or Jotuns instead of and as well as the Aesir. To say nothing of other, more popular religions. </div> </div> </div>But the Aesir and Vanir might not even be spirits in Werewolf (especially since WW decided to make a connection between Odin and a Gangrel 4th gen), and Apocalypse presented jotun as a group of beings that weren't wholly spirit or flesh and were just rivals to Garou. Revised did some very heavy deconstruction on some old, established orders of the game, and the Get probably had the biggest change done; while these changes may seem trivial to you, they were rather directly made to put human veneration of anything, as blind and ignorant as it is presented as in Werewolf on account of how humans don't know much about spirits, overwhelmingly in the wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think our differences in opinion come down to some very fundimentaly different takes on the setting. Werewolf just strikes me as a tragic setting more then a horror one. In that you are empowered but that power is ultimately worthless against the true enemy and your doomed to fail. </div> </div> </div>No, the power is not worthless. You just have to not use it like your ancestors did, which requires going against a lot of traditions. And by not use it like your ancestors did, I mean not just the &quot;think bigger&quot; caveat, but also not buying into propaganda about the War of Rage or repeating its mistakes, and making sure that your rampages are much better timed and much more surgical. Which is difficult, because Rage seems to strike like Stress problems in Darkest Dungeon. Actually, lots of problems in W:tA can crop up like problems in DD... slowly, insidious, and difficult, if not impossible to stop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't find any personal horror in being a Fera, &quot;So I'm a holy warrior for nature? Corporate suits really are out to destroy the world and I have to stop them? I get super powers? Sign me up!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Never assume that I mean personal horror when I type out the word horror on its own. That is very specifically Vampire's thing. Werewolf says &quot;Savage Horror&quot; right on the inside front cover, and per the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, this carries certain assumptions that tend to weigh the world's inhabitants toward Made of Plasticine. Sure, Garou can wade through most small arms fire without suffering much, if any, injury as long as it isn't silver, but when they start to claw and bite, limbs fall to the ground, flesh and blood go flying, and the end result looks a lot like the brown bear attack on the soldiers in chapter 10 of Golden Kamuy, or any given play-through in Doom (2016) that makes liberal use of glory kills and chainsaw attacks. It's adrenaline-charged, it can even be exciting, but then it happens to people you care about, either because the characters lose control (less used in W:tA because, again, V:tM has a pretty tight hold on personal horror) or because their enemies go to town on the characters' allies in the same fashion. Rage ensues, but doesn't change that it manages to hit the characters and cause damage in ways that they can't soak.<br /> <br /> Also, Fera is not a broadly encompassing term that includes Garou. It is the Garou word for Changers that aren't Garou. It replaced the similarly off use of Bete, which showed up in the oddest places and uttered by the strangest folk for a term that is the Mokole word for Changers that aren't Mokole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T09:08:02-07:00","id":1142927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142829#post1142829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Existence independently of belief is mostly orthogonal to religion.<br /> Taking Moses' word as true, Moses saw proof of YHWH existing independently of his belief; does that make Moses irreligious or unfaithful? No, because otherwise you're forced to discard lots and lots of key figures in religions as irreligious/unfaithful.<br /> Conversely, I have faith that what my senses tell me about the existence of an outside world to be <i>somewhat</i> true. If I had no faith in that, I would be a solipsist. But again, that does not make me religious about, say, my ability to see this keyboard I'm typing with.<br /> <br /> Just because Garou religion is not at all similar to Abrahamic religions, but rather to animistic and other religions that treat relationships with deities as a more egalitarian affair, does not make Garou irreligious. In fact to dismiss Garou ways as irreligious is to go No True Scotsman on huge swathes of non-'Western' religions (and surely some of the older 'Western' ones), particularly most animistic ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tack on religion in the Revised ST Handbook notes that religion will mean something different in a game of Werewolf on account of what they absolutely know. Specifics involving Gaia are there, but day to day dealings with spirits are However, there's also a sidebar noting that if religion isn't a topic that the table feels like tackling, you can drop it and play without any trappings of it. Which may be weird to broader cultural theory, but still stands as a thing that you can do, and may need to do in order to keep a game together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of that seems to disqualify them of being religious. They just follow a religion that differs from human ones. </div> </div> </div>Mostly about trying to fill in the blanks on bigger picture stuff. Which is why they've been slow to execute bigger picture stuff, most likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:05:52-07:00","id":1142950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142924#post1142924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But correcting its ailment was apparently possible in that one Apocalypse scenario... provided that you were allies with Gurahl and brought along other Fera to help find the way to the proper ritual space with the least amount of fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confused by this answer. It doesn't really connect to the debate over whether or not Garou and (by extention of your implication that Garou are not religious because they are animist) irl animists are religious or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142924#post1142924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nowhere near the frame that the Fenrir work with now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer literally every other edition (1st,2nd or 20th) to revisied. I apologise, I should have made that known when I made my initial point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142924#post1142924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Aesir and Vanir might not even be spirits in Werewolf (especially since WW decided to make a connection between Odin and a Gangrel 4th gen), and Apocalypse presented jotun as a group of beings that weren't wholly spirit or flesh and were just rivals to Garou. Revised did some very heavy deconstruction on some old, established orders of the game, and the Get probably had the biggest change done; while these changes may seem trivial to you, they were rather directly made to put human veneration of anything, as blind and ignorant as it is presented as in Werewolf on account of how humans don't know much about spirits, overwhelmingly in the wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again your missing the forest for the trees. My point was that both my self, my co-religionists and the Garou have an animistic worldview and worship those animistic forces. You have been asserting (since post #34) that they are not religious (specificly not a religious holy order of warriors) because this seemingly does not match your view of what a religion is. I am attempting to convince you otherwise. Without success I must admit.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Please tell me if i've misunderstood you somewhere along the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142924#post1142924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never assume that I mean personal horror when I type out the word horror on its own. That is very specifically Vampire's thing. Werewolf says &quot;Savage Horror&quot; right on the inside front cover, and per the Revised Storyteller's Handbook, this carries certain assumptions that tend to weigh the world's inhabitants toward Made of Plasticine. Sure, Garou can wade through most small arms fire without suffering much, if any, injury as long as it isn't silver, but when they start to claw and bite, limbs fall to the ground, flesh and blood go flying, and the end result looks a lot like the brown bear attack on the soldiers in chapter 10 of Golden Kamuy, or any given play-through in Doom (2016) that makes liberal use of glory kills and chainsaw attacks. It's adrenaline-charged, it can even be exciting, but then it happens to people you care about, either because the characters lose control (less used in W:tA because, again, V:tM has a pretty tight hold on personal horror) or because their enemies go to town on the characters' allies in the same fashion. Rage ensues, but doesn't change that it manages to hit the characters and cause damage in ways that they can't soak.<br /> <br /> Also, Fera is not a broadly encompassing term that includes Garou. It is the Garou word for Changers that aren't Garou. It replaced the similarly off use of Bete, which showed up in the oddest places and uttered by the strangest folk for a term that is the Mokole word for Changers that aren't Mokole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I hadn't realised that. Thanks for telling me.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:17:05-07:00","id":1142954,"title":"","content":"I usually use real-life history to guide my WoD games (with some anime stylized tropes thrown in), but shy away from current events for the sake of good taste.<br /> <br /> In my WoD, the gang wars of today are just as bad as it was in the 1980's and 1990's, perhaps even moreso. In an upcoming Chicago By Night 1e game, I want to incorporate the gang cultures and history of Chicago's underworld into the plot, and have all the major gangs represented whether they be People or Folks, Black, Latino, or White, but I'm unsure if I should use the actual names and histories of Chicago gangs or do the Grand Theft Auto approach of taking a real gang, but changing the name and altering certain historical details to fit artistic license (for example, in GTA IV, the Latin Kings are renamed the Spanish Lords and the Gambino Crime Family is renamed the Gambetti Crime Family, with John Gotti being replaced by Jon Gravelli. It's essentially the same basic archetype, but names are changed for legal, artistic, and other reasons.)<br /> <br /> Considering the fact I am running the Chicago chronicle for my college's gaming club, I am leaning towards taking the &quot;GTA approach&quot; to the gang wars. Sort of like how Johnny Fontane in The Godfather is not Frank Sinatra, but is an obvious stand-in for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T10:38:13-07:00","id":1142965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142950#post1142950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused by this answer. It doesn't really connect to the debate over whether or not Garou and (by extention of your implication that Garou are not religious because they are animist) irl animists are religious or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I prefer literally every other edition (1st,2nd or 20th) to revisied. I apologise, I should have made that known when I made my initial point. </div> </div> </div>W20 uses an awful lot of Revised, and keeps going in the general direction, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again your missing the forest for the trees. </div> </div> </div>There is no more forest. Medieval Europeans cut it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point was that both my self, my co-religionists and the Garou have an animistic worldview and worship those animistic forces. You have been asserting (since post #34) that they are not religious (specificly not a religious holy order of warriors) because this seemingly does not match your view of what a religion is. I am attempting to convince you otherwise. Without success I must admit.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Please tell me if i've misunderstood you somewhere along the way. </div> </div> </div>As per my post responding to vicky_molokh, you don't need to use religion, so its presence in Werewolf is arguably going to be soft to invisible. At the very least, nowhere near what the original assertion suggested, particularly since the poster that made it was under the impression that every Stargazer was somehow a Buddhist monk, and claimed that the book explicitly mentioned that they were a religious military order, which would tend to make the presentation of the Dies Ultimae camp of Glass Walkers somewhat redundant if that were the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T10:08:58-07:00","id":1143264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1142927#post1142927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tack on religion in the Revised ST Handbook notes that religion will mean something different in a game of Werewolf on account of what they absolutely know. Specifics involving Gaia are there, but day to day dealings with spirits are However, there's also a sidebar noting that if religion isn't a topic that the table feels like tackling, you can drop it and play without any trappings of it. Which may be weird to broader cultural theory, but still stands as a thing that you can do, and may need to do in order to keep a game together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly about trying to fill in the blanks on bigger picture stuff. Which is why they've been slow to execute bigger picture stuff, most likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please rephrase your reply? Because I don't quite understand what you mean by 'tack on' in this context. Werewolves deal with deities all the time, such as learning Gifts from spider-spirits, or scaring a spirit of sharpness out of a knife to make it behave as if blunt. That makes them religious animists at <b>a minimum</b>. There's no tacking on involved because religion is <b>already</b> all-permeating in the Werewolf game line. To remove religion from Werewolf is to remove 80%-95% of what Werewolf is about<b></b>: no Gifts, no Umbra, no spirits, no rituals, no Apocalypse, no struggle. It's not a topic you can avoid without ripping out everything that makes WtA WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T10:44:52-07:00","id":1143275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1143264#post1143264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please rephrase your reply? Because I don't quite understand what you mean by 'tack on' in this context. Werewolves deal with deities all the time, such as learning Gifts from spider-spirits, or scaring a spirit of sharpness out of a knife to make it behave as if blunt. That makes them religious animists at <b>a minimum</b>. There's no tacking on involved because religion is <b>already</b> all-permeating in the Werewolf game line. To remove religion from Werewolf is to remove 80%-95% of what Werewolf is about<b></b>: no Gifts, no Umbra, no spirits, no rituals, no Apocalypse, no struggle. It's not a topic you can avoid without ripping out everything that makes WtA WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tack on something is a synonym for an interpretation, possibly as some odd variation of the &quot;take&quot; on something. It has nothing to do with tacking on or affixing. I'm not sure why this wasn't at least contextually clear, since the statements that followed that colloquialism didn't have much to do with the affixing definition, but lept straight into talking about the material.<br /> <br /> (Also, there is no spirit of sharpness in a knife. There is a spirit of the knife, which has sharpness as an essential quality, and the various gifts that keep it from working as a knife seem to have a variety of ways of accomplishing this end.)<br /> <br /> You're free to interpret Garou and Fera as religious. The book also says that you're free to interpret them as not religious, especially if your group has very strong opinions about religion or what constitutes religion. Note that the game also tends to answer that question that it tries to present as being mysterious - who or what Gaia is - in the core book by giving a default assumption that She is the spirit of the entire cosmos and, accordingly, more important than anything else. Anything that diverges from this is technically non-canonical, so notions of the game's setup being religion tend to fall by the wayside and end up as facts of life and interaction, especially since the Garou and Fera are half-spirit and hence kin to the other side of existence. Is it a religion if a god is entreating and communicating with other gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T08:36:35-07:00","id":1143801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1143275#post1143275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tack on something is a synonym for an interpretation, possibly as some odd variation of the &quot;take&quot; on something. It has nothing to do with tacking on or affixing. I'm not sure why this wasn't at least contextually clear, since the statements that followed that colloquialism didn't have much to do with the affixing definition, but lept straight into talking about the material.<br /> <br /> (Also, there is no spirit of sharpness in a knife. There is a spirit of the knife, which has sharpness as an essential quality, and the various gifts that keep it from working as a knife seem to have a variety of ways of accomplishing this end.)<br /> <br /> You're free to interpret Garou and Fera as religious. The book also says that you're free to interpret them as not religious, especially if your group has very strong opinions about religion or what constitutes religion. Note that the game also tends to answer that question that it tries to present as being mysterious - who or what Gaia is - in the core book by giving a default assumption that She is the spirit of the entire cosmos and, accordingly, more important than anything else. Anything that diverges from this is technically non-canonical, so notions of the game's setup being religion tend to fall by the wayside and end up as facts of life and interaction, especially since the Garou and Fera are half-spirit and hence kin to the other side of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't see where any interpretation is in the matter. The books allegedly claim that Garou are possibly irreligious . . . while the books <i>blatantly and explicitly</i> describe how Garou regularly deal with various deities when conducting rituals, learning gifts, or making that knife stop working as a knife.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1143275#post1143275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is it a religion if a god is entreating and communicating with other gods?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Of course. These are <i>gods</i> after all. If they weren't gods, we could talk about it not being religion (but not all religions include gods - for instance, there are variants of Buddhism that are atheistic; I'm thinking there may be other godless religions).</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T21:17:28-07:00","id":1144282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1143801#post1143801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see where any interpretation is in the matter. The books allegedly claim that Garou are possibly irreligious . . . while the books <i>blatantly and explicitly</i> describe how Garou regularly deal with various deities when conducting rituals, learning gifts, or making that knife stop working as a knife.</div> </div> </div> </div>MY suggestion is that they put that disclaimer that you don't have to play it as religious if you don't want to (Which implies it is by default religious) to prevent too many American Christians getting super upset like with D&amp;D in the 80s<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T22:41:18-07:00","id":1144290,"title":"","content":"&quot;Garou are an order of holy warriors&quot; is, at the very least, intensely misleading. It tends to conjure up images of Knights Templar or Souhei that don't quite fit so well (Souhei fits slightly more, but not quite as well as one might imagine). You typically need to get into Camps to have those trappings proper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1144282#post1144282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MY suggestion is that they put that disclaimer that you don't have to play it as religious if you don't want to (Which implies it is by default religious) to prevent too many American Christians getting super upset like with D&amp;D in the 80s</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would they wait to do that until Revised? Prior editions were actually quite scanty on religious treatments at all, other than that human religions were all wrong and that churches are potential fronts for monster hunters or other monsters. W:tA wasn't exactly high profile, either; it's never really gotten much media coverage, and people outside of tabletop gaming circles are not liable to pick it out from a lineup if D&amp;D is present, as D&amp;D is tabletop rpgs in the minds of most people, and D&amp;D is always present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T23:47:33-07:00","id":1144301,"title":"","content":"1) Because they didn't think of it at the time<br /> 2) They had complaints and wanted to prevent more<br /> <br /> I don't have the wording, but if they said anything along the lines of &quot;you don't have to if you don't want to&quot; then linguistically that implies the opposite to be true unless an explicit decision is made.<br /> Like the Golden rule, you can change the rules; still means the rest are the normal rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T20:31:25-07:00","id":1144617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1134438-real-world-vs-world-of-darkness?p=1144301#post1144301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Because they didn't think of it at the time</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) They had complaints and wanted to prevent more </div> </div> </div>I still have doubts about that. Like I said, where's the trail on the public outrage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't have the wording, but if they said anything along the lines of &quot;you don't have to if you don't want to&quot; then linguistically that implies the opposite to be true unless an explicit decision is made.<br /> Like the Golden rule, you can change the rules; still means the rest are the normal rules </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things that the text emphasizes in the book, and religion or a religious approach can kind of easily fade into the background. Religion as an approach doesn't even get much word count until accessory books, so the sidebar seems to be giving any group that didn't think of it before hand a clean bill of health and a &quot;don't worry, just play your way&quot; message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T18:30:36-07:00","id":1145933,"title":"","content":"[How about we get back to the original topic, instead of perpetuating quote wars and fights over semantics and definitions, yeah?]<br /> <br /> <br /> Pentex, for me, is a corporation who primarily differs from other corporations in two important ways: 1) they destroy the planet and sow corruption consciously, as an end unto it, rather than through negligence; and 2) they have access to supernatural power and some understanding thereof, because they are buddy buddy with the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> A vast majority of the damage Pentex does is the same damage all industrial companies do. They pollute, they peddle unhealthy products, they put employees and civilians through unsafe and degrading conditions, etc. They make the world a worse place, even while theoretically they do good. They differ from other corporations in that, when faced with a business choice between two options, Pentex values not just what is most profitable, but also what will bring about the end of the world faster. Sometimes, the former can be sacrificed in favor of the latter; since Pentex is so huge, it can afford to take losses here and there and still remain comfortably afloat.<br /> <br /> For instance, they will open two O'Tolley's restaurants within a short distance from each other. Even though the cost of running two might not outstrip the profit, Pentex would see &quot;raising obesity rates by making O'Tolley's more convenient than other food places&quot; as a valid goal to work towards.<br /> <br /> Speaking of O'Tolley's, it illustrates my next point. I don't think Pentex puts Banes in every consumer product. Making millions of people Fomori overnight might seem desirable, but it would also give up the game and hurt Pentex's efforts in the long run. At the very least, a company that did that on a wide scale would make enemies of every other supernatural group (vampires want to protect the Masquerade, the Technocracy wants to better the world and protect the Consensus and generally foster consumer confidence in modern Capitalism, most Traditions would have moral or practical objections, the Garou could come dangerously close to getting more allies for themselves and their cause, etc.).<br /> <br /> Nor does Pentex NEED to put Banes in everything. As the W20 Book of the Wyrm points out, O'Tolley's promotes corruption, misery, poor health, death, and all that Wyrm stuff perfectly well, just from selling cheap, greasy food in a convenient way for the common person. Banes are already attracted to such places, because fast food joints promote all these ills, providing a fertile breeding ground for slow decline for the world. This is most of what Pentex does: provide products that people want, in such a way that is good in the short term but bad in the long term. I can also imagine Magadon being behind the proliferation of Opioid drugs, as it technically provides a medical use, but also leads to widespread addiction that ruins people's lives. All while seemingly helping people.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say Pentex never creates Bane-laden products. I think they do. But those are side projects, rather than products with wide commercial availability.<br /> <br /> For instance, Pentex might produce a certain quantity of cigarettes that are cut with Banes. They come in cool black packs, and rolled in black paper. Minimal or zero product labels, and no health information...or warnings. At best, it might have an ironic, tongue-in-cheek skull design on the front. Pentex does not sell these in stores, and indeed the products aren't approved or overseen by any regulatory agency. Instead, they are sold (or, at least at first, given away) to individual people, by individual folks who push them in informal settings. If an employee in a Pentex-controlled company is known to smoke, one of their coworkers or someone higher up might turn them on to these mysterious black cigs.<br /> <br /> And why wouldn't someone smoke them, if they already have the habit? They go down smooth, have a rich flavor, and (according to Pentex's shills) have some kind of chemical additive that slows chemical reactions of the nicotine in the cigarettes, making it so they can pack more nicotine in every cig without killing the user. In the end, a cigarette that is worth several other cigarettes, allowing them to smoke less to get their daily fix (since, allegedly, one cig will have the smoker absorbing nicotine all day long). Sure, this designer &quot;brand&quot; costs more than single packs of common cigs...but is still cheaper in aggregate, because they cost less than a carton of store brands, the user can smoke fewer to get their fix, and the black market nature of it means they aren't subject to the taxes that inflate prices so much.<br /> <br /> So when Pentex offers it to select individuals - including folks who work for them in more...secretive capacities - they quickly get hooked. Dependent, even, since the stronger, higher quality nature of the product is so good, the smoker quickly becomes incapable of going back to inferior commercial cigs. They need the Good Stuff; once they go black, they can never go back. Which turns them from a simple money-maker into a method of controlling people. &quot;Sure I can get you more...but my supplies are limited this month, friend. Maybe if you do me and my employers a favor, I can bump you to the top of the waiting list.&quot;<br /> <br /> Over time, the smoker is changed from just a customer into a cultivated agent. An agent who will soon become even more valuable, as the spiritual corruption settles in and turns them into a Fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}